$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of Benzyl Alcohol to Benzaldehyde:
Typical Procedure: To a vigorously stirred kieselguhr (2 g) Jones reagent
[61 (0.4 mL, 3.3 mmol) is added slowly until the orange powder are
produced. CH2Cl2 (10mL) is added to the obtained mixture. A solution of
benzyl alcohol (108 mg, 1 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) is then added slowly to
the above stirred heterogeneous mixture at room temperature for 10 min.
The progress of the reaction is monitored by TLC (aluminumbacked silica
gel Merck 60 GF254 plates) using hexane-ethyl acetate (8:2) as eluent.
The solid is filtered and washed with CH2Cl2 (3x5 mL). The combined
filtrates are evaporated to give crude product, which is purified by
preparative TLC with hexane.ethyl acetate (8:2). 103 mg (97%)
benzaldehyde. Product: PhC(O)Ph; Yield: 97%. b.p.(°C/mm): Found:
117-119/0.9; Reported: 305°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Kieselguhr supported Jones reagent as agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A new efficient oxidation of alcohols with Jones reagent supported on
Kieselguhr
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lou, Ji-Dong; Ma, Yi-Chun; Gao, Chun-Ling; Li, Li
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis and Reactivity in Inorganic, Metal-Organic, and Nano-Metal
Chemistry (2006), 36(5), 381-383

