$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Oxidation of Benzyl Alcohol to Benzaldehyde: Typical Procedure: To a
vigorously stirred kieselguhr (2 g) Jones reagent [61 (0.4 mL, 3.3 mmol)
is added slowly until the orange powder are produced. CH2Cl2 (10mL) is
added to the obtained mixture. A solution of benzyl alcohol (108 mg, 1
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) is then added slowly to the above stirred
heterogeneous mixture at room temperature for 10 min. The progress of the
reaction is monitored by TLC (aluminumbacked silica gel Merck 60 GF254
plates) using hexane-ethyl acetate (8:2) as eluent. The solid is filtered
and washed with CH2Cl2 (3x5 mL). The combined filtrates are evaporated to
give crude product, which is purified by preparative TLC with
hexane.ethyl acetate (8:2). 103 mg (97%) benzaldehyde. Product: PhCHO;
Yield: 97%. b.p.(°C/mm): Found: 56-58/10; Reported: 178-179°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Kieselguhr supported Jones reagent as agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A new efficient oxidation of alcohols with Jones reagent supported on
Kieselguhr
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lou, Ji-Dong; Ma, Yi-Chun; Gao, Chun-Ling; Li, Li
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis and Reactivity in Inorganic, Metal-Organic, and Nano-Metal
Chemistry (2006), 36(5), 381-383

