$DATUM 6-Phenyl-1-[(2S,3S,4S,5R,6S)-tetrahyro-3,4,5,6-tetramethoxypyran-2-yl]hexane-1,4-dione
(29). DMSO (0.09 mL, 1.27 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) was added dropwise to
a stirred and cooled (-78 °C) solution of (COCl)2 (0.06 mL, 0.694 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (1 mL). After 15 min, a solution of 28 (101.6 mg, 0.255 mmol)
in CH2Cl2 (1.5 mL) was added dropwise, and stirring at -78 °C was
continued for 35 min. Then Et3N (0.2 mL) was added dropwise, and stirring
at -78 °C was continued for 5 min. The cooling bath was removed, and
stirring was continued for 25 min. Water (2 mL) was added, and the
organic phase was dried (MgSO4) and evaporated. Flash chromatography of
the residue over silica gel (1.5 x 13 cm), using 50% EtOAc-hexanes, gave
29 (83.9 mg, 83%) as an colorless oil.
6-Phenyl-1-[(2S,3S,4S,5R,6S)-tetrahyro-3,4,5,6-tetramethoxypyran-2-yl]hexane-1,4-dione
(29), yield 83.9 mg, 83% [α] 20 D 79.2 (c 1.35, CHCl3); FTIR (CHCl3, cast
microscope) 3062, 3027, 2933, 2836, 1716, 1604, 1497, 1454 cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 2.60- 2.68 (m, 1 H), 2.72-2.85 (m, 4 H), 2.89-3.03 (m,
3 H), 3.20- 3.31 (m, 2 H), 3.45-3.63 (m, 13 H), 4.06 (dd, J = 1.6, 10 Hz,
1 H), 4.87 (dd, J = 1.6, 3.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.17-7.21 (m, 3 H), 7.26-7.30 (m,
2 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 30.0 (t), 34.7 (t), 36.0 (t), 44.5 (t),
55.9 (q), 59.4 (q), 60.8 (q), 61.2 (q), 74.0 (d), 80.9 (d), 81.5 (d),
83.7 (d), 98.1 (d), 126.3 (d), 128.5 (d), 128.7 (d), 141.2 (s), 205.8
(s), 208.2 (s); exact mass m/z calcd for C21H30NaO7 (M + Na) 417.1884,
found 417.1879.
