$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (b) Tetradecanedial (23)6a. (COCl)2 (0.36 mL, 4.1 mmol) was added
dropwise to a stirred and cooled (-78 °C) solution of DMSO (0.5800, 8.163
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL). After 15 min, a solution of 23b (0.122 mL, 0.529
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (3 mL) was added dropwise. After a further 45 min, Et3N
(1.474 mL, 10.57 mmol) was added dropwise, and stirring was continued for
30 min. The mixture was then stored at -20 °C (freezer) for 20 h,
transferred to an ice bath, and stirred at 0 °C for 3 h. Water (6 mL) and
CH2Cl2 (10 mL) were added, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic extracts were washed with saturated aqueous
NaHCO3, dried (MgSO4) and evaporated. Flash chromatography of the residue
over silica gel (1.4 x 16 cm), using EtOAc-petroleum ether mixtures from
5% to 15% EtOAc, gave 23 (0.0901 g, 83%) as an oil. Tetradecanedial (23),
yield 0.0901 g, 83% FTIR (CH2Cl2, cast) 2915, 2850, 2749, 1788, 1705,
1674, 1471 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.23-1.37 (m, 16 H), 1.63
(quintet, J = 7.2 Hz, 4 H), 2.42 (td, J = 7.4, 1.9 Hz, 4 H), 9.77 (t, J =
1.9 Hz, 2 H); 13C NMR(CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 22.1 (t), 29.2 (t), 29.3 (t),
29.4 (t), 29.5 (t), 43.9 (t), 202.9 (d); exact mass m/z calcd for
C14H26NaO2 (M + Na) 249.1825, found 249.1828.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM second, third and fourth stages dropwise addition; fifthstage quench,
Swern oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Conversion of 1,4-Diketones into para-Disubstituted Benzenes
