$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Cycloheptyl-4-cyclohexylbutane-1,4-dione (18). Jones reagent20 (7.0 Min
acetone, 0.17 mL, 1.2 mmol)was added dropwise to a stirred and cooled (0
°C) solution of 17 (0.0346 g, 0.129 mmol) in acetone (10 mL). After 1.5
h, an additional portion of Jones reagent (7.0 Min acetone, 0.10 mL, 0.70
mmol) was added, and after a further 5 min, the mixture was quenched with
MeOH (15 mL). Stirring was continued for 30 min, by which time the
mixture had become dark green. The mixture was diluted with EtOAc (25
mL), washed with water and brine, dried (Na2SO4), and evaporated. Flash
chromatography of the residue over silica gel (0.7 x 16 cm), using
EtOAcpetroleum ether mixtures from 5% to 15% EtOAc, gave 18 (0.0239 g,
70%) as an oil. 1-Cycloheptyl-4-cyclohexylbutane-1,4-dione (18), yield
0.0239 g, 70% FTIR (CH2Cl2, microscope) 2928, 2855, 2668, 1707, 1450
cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz) δ 1.10-1.43 (m, 6 H), 1.43-1.65 (m, 6 H),
1.65-1.83 (m, 6 H), 1.83-1.94 (m, 4 H), 2.32-2.44 (m, 1 H), 2.52-2.62 (m,
1 H), 2.66-2.75 (m, 4 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125MHz) δ 25.7 (t), 25.9 (t),
26.7 (t), 28.3 (t), 28.5 (t), 30.0 (t), 34.1 (t), 34.2 (t), 50.8 (d),
52.4 (d), 212.8 (s), 213.1 (s); exact mass m/z calcd for C17H28O2
264.2089, found 264.2090.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM second and third stages dropwise addn. of reagent; fourth stage quench,
Jones reagent used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Conversion of 1,4-Diketones into para-Disubstituted Benzenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
